/-! ## §4. Adversarial gate (product enrichment refused) -/

/-- Named refusal: unconstrained product enrichment
(`PostingEnrichedPathClass` = `ExactPathClass × Fin 8`) is **not** an
inhabitant of `PostingHistoryContinuumData` for continuum-close purposes
without discharging `generatedByActualPostingTransaction` and
`pushforward_mu` from actual posting-transaction provenance.

This is an API honesty gate linked to STOP A
(`carrier_forgets_posting_phase`): the forgetful product erases posting
phase under descent and cannot be laundered into continuum data by
setting the generation Prop to `True`. -/
def AdversarialGate_unconstrainedProductRefused : Prop :=
  ¬ FactorsThroughPostingForget fun _n H => postingPhase H

/-- The adversarial gate holds by STOP A (carrier forgets posting phase). -/
theorem adversarialGate_unconstrainedProductRefused :
    AdversarialGate_unconstrainedProductRefused :=
  postingPhase_not_factors_through_forget

/-- Packaging note: any continuum-data candidate built from product
enrichment must still face the generation + pushforward fields; the
STOP A forgetfulness theorem remains the discriminator against fake
descent. -/
theorem continuumData_refuses_forgetful_product_descent :
    TypedResidual_carrier_forgets_posting_phase :=
  typedResidual_carrier_forgets_posting_phase

